  "content": {
    "id": "p34-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Bob has $n$ lollies in his left pocket and $n$ lollies in his right pocket. He reaches into both pockets simultaneously and pulls out $k$ lollies with each hand, then eats exactly one lolly from each hand.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p34-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "For a fixed $k$, how many ways can Bob pull out $k$ lollies from each pocket and then eat one from each hand?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k^2\\binom{n}{k}^{2}$ ways.",
          "worked": "For each pocket, choose $k$ lollies in $\\binom{n}{k}$ ways, then choose the lolly eaten in $k$ ways. The choices for the two pockets are independent.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Number of ways}&=\\left(k\\binom{n}{k}\\right)^2\\\\\\text{Number of ways}&=k^2\\binom{n}{k}^{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p34-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Suppose a lolly is first eaten from each pocket, before $k-1$ lollies are pulled out from each pocket. How many ways can this be done?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$n^2\\binom{n-1}{k-1}^{2}$ ways.",
          "worked": "For each pocket, choose the lolly eaten in $n$ ways, then choose $k-1$ lollies from the remaining $n-1$ in $\\binom{n-1}{k-1}$ ways. The choices for the two pockets are independent.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Number of ways}&=\\left(n\\binom{n-1}{k-1}\\right)^2\\\\\\text{Number of ways}&=n^2\\binom{n-1}{k-1}^{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p34-q14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Hence, find a simple expression for\n$$1^2\\binom{n}{1}^{2}+2^2\\binom{n}{2}^{2}+\\cdots+n^2\\binom{n}{n}^{2}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p34-q14-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "n^2\\binom{2n-2}{n-1}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p34-q14-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Equate the counts in (a) and (b), sum over ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "k=1,\\ldots,n",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", then apply question 13 with ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "n-1",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " in place of ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "n",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Parts (a) and (b) count the same outcomes: in each pocket, one lolly is eaten and $k-1$ other lollies are selected. Therefore,\n$$k^2\\binom{n}{k}^{2}=n^2\\binom{n-1}{k-1}^{2}.$$\nSumming for $k=1,\\ldots,n$ and writing $r=k-1$ gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sum_{k=1}^{n}k^2\\binom{n}{k}^{2}&=n^2\\sum_{k=1}^{n}\\binom{n-1}{k-1}^{2}\\\\\\sum_{k=1}^{n}k^2\\binom{n}{k}^{2}&=n^2\\sum_{r=0}^{n-1}\\binom{n-1}{r}^{2}\\\\\\sum_{k=1}^{n}k^2\\binom{n}{k}^{2}&=n^2\\binom{2n-2}{n-1}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe last equality uses question 13 with $n-1$ in place of $n$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      }
    ]
  },
